# Security

- Access token, refresh token, and session payload go through `flutter_secure_storage` (`SessionStorage` / `SecureStorageService`) only. Never `SharedPreferences`, never source constants.

```dart
// BAD
prefs.setString('access_token', token);

// GOOD
await sessionStorage.saveTokens(accessToken: token, refreshToken: refresh);
```

- `AuthInterceptor` attaches Bearer, refreshes on 401 (once, loop-capped), and on refresh failure calls `onSessionExpired`. It must not `context.go()`, throw for the UI to catch, or navigate. `authGuardRedirect` is the only auth-driven navigation (login / splash / `SessionExpiredPage`).
- Logout clears **every** credential, not only the access token, and resets the **session owner** (`authSessionProvider` on Riverpod, `AuthCubit`/`AuthBloc` on BLoC).
- Do not log passwords, tokens, GPS, national IDs, or license payloads — including debug. Release builds: no pretty HTTP logger, obfuscation (`--obfuscate`) when preparing a release.
- Government/military endpoints require certificate pinning in `lib/core/network/` before the feature is done.
- Screens that show classified, licensed, or PII data: screenshot/screen-recording prevention. Session auto-lock, when required, must re-enter the same session-owner flow — not a second lock screen. Compromised-device checks, when required, are treated as unauthenticated on protected routes via the same guard.
